{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q355210","formula":"CaMgAsO₄(OH)","hill":"AsCaHMgO5","elements":["H","O","Mg","Ca","As"],"composition":{"H":1.0,"O":5.0,"As":1.0,"Ca":1.0,"Mg":1.0},"names":{"en":"Adelite","ru":"Аделит","uk":"Аделіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"The rare mineral adelite, is a calcium, magnesium, arsenate with chemical formula CaMgAsO4OH. It forms a solid solution series with the vanadium-bearing mineral gottlobite. Various transition metals substitute for magnesium and lead replaces calcium leading to a variety of similar minerals in the adelite–duftite group. Adelite forms variably colored (blue, green, yellow and grey) crystals in the orthorhombic crystal system.","ru":"Аделит — редкий минерал, основный арсенат кальция и магния. Название происходит от греч. άδηλος — «неясный, неразличимый» (из-за того, что иногда бывает непрозрачным).","uk":"Аделі́т (рос. аделит; англ. adelite; нім."},"fame":20,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q355210","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adelite.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q408114","formula":"CaZnAsO₄(OH)","names":{"en":"Austinite","uk":"Аустиніт"},"elements":["H","O","Ca","Zn","As"],"fame":14,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q4280210",